## Why This Is Asked

Tests per-tenant Saga resilience, isolation, and recovery with Event Sourcing and outbox.

## Key Concepts

- CQRS and Event Sourcing
- Saga orchestration and compensations
- Per-tenant isolation and outbox pattern
- Idempotent event handlers and replay

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch (pseudo)
function startSaga(tenantId, jobId){
  dispatchEvent({tenantId, jobId, type:'IngestRequested'});
}
function onEvent(event){
  if(event.type==='IngestSucceeded') emit('TranscodeRequested', event);
  if(event.type==='IngestFailed' || event.type==='TranscodeFailed' || event.type==='WatermarkFailed'){
    emit('Compensate', {tenantId:event.tenantId, jobId:event.jobId, steps:['Ingest','Transcode','Watermark']});
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you ensure exactly-once processing for the tenant outbox?
- How would you test failure injection and crash recovery in this Saga?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly, real-world saga with event-sourcing and CQRS: how to coordinate cross-service work, model event contracts, and ensure idempotent handlers with an outbox.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography in a write-side workflow
- Event contracts and read-model sketching for status tracking
- Outbox pattern and correlation-based deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
// Map write events to commands (simplified)
function mapEventToCommand(evt){
  switch(evt.type){
    case 'ContentSubmitted':
      return { type: 'ModerationRequest', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId, correlationId: evt.id } }
    case 'ModerationApproved':
      return { type: 'PublishContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
    case 'ModerationRejected':
      return { type: 'HideContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
  }
}

// Deduplication (idempotent handler)
if (outbox.has(correlationId)) return; outbox.add(correlationId);
```

